      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Since $6b \\equiv 3+b \\pmod 7,$ it follows by subtracting $b$ from both sides and dividing by 3 that $2b \\equiv 3 \\pmod 7.$  Then $b$ is a positive integer less than 7 such that $2b = 3 + 7k$ for some integer $k.$\n\nIf $b = 1,$ then the possibilities for $b$ are $b = 1$ or $b = 4.$ Check them.\n\n- If $b = 1,$ then $a \\equiv 5 \\pmod 7.$\n- If $b = 4,$ then $6(4) = 24 \\equiv 3 \\not\\equiv 7k + 1 \\pmod 7.$\n\nThus, $b = 1$ and $a \\equiv 5 \\pmod 7.$\n\nFinally, since $5c \\equiv 2 \\pmod 7,$ we have $c \\equiv 2 \\cdot 5^{-1} \\equiv 2 \\cdot 3 \\equiv 6 \\pmod 7.$\n\nBecause $a,b,c$ are all less than 7, it follows that $a+b+c \\equiv 5 + 1 + 6 \\equiv 2 \\pmod 7.$\nThe answer is 2",
